This almost sounds deliberate -- it lets you cross a narrow stretch of
lava using non-fireproof water walking boots, as long as you're
desperate enough to be willing to sacrifice the boots.

One could imagine the sequence of events going like this:

  You step onto the lava.
  Your boots magically stop you from sinking!
  Your boots catch fire!
  You quickly jump off the lava, leaving the smoldering remains of
  your boots behind.

However, I agree that the fact that you don't start sinking even if
you linger on the lava is definitely a bug.  Similarly, deliberately
removing your boots while standing on lava should certainly make you
start sinking immediately.

